{"video_id": "ldpDNtPC_mU", "channel_id": "UCqwkX8ZieryoPmcupkpcXRA", "fetched_at": "2026-10-02T06:22:28.876964+00:00", "fetch_tool": "yt-dlp 2026.08.19", "caption_track_type": "auto_generated", "segments": [{"start_seconds": 5.84, "end_seconds": 10.64, "text": "Hi everyone. Welcome back. In today's"}, {"start_seconds": 8.4, "end_seconds": 13.48, "text": "session, we will learn one of the most"}, {"start_seconds": 10.64, "end_seconds": 16.72, "text": "powerful reshaping tools in Pandas, and"}, {"start_seconds": 13.48, "end_seconds": 19.04, "text": "that is melt method. It helps you turn"}, {"start_seconds": 16.72, "end_seconds": 20.8, "text": "wide data into long data, perfect for"}, {"start_seconds": 19.04, "end_seconds": 22.8, "text": "plotting, analytics, and machine"}, {"start_seconds": 20.8, "end_seconds": 25.2, "text": "learning pre-processing."}, {"start_seconds": 22.8, "end_seconds": 27.68, "text": "So, let's jump right in."}, {"start_seconds": 25.2, "end_seconds": 31.44, "text": "Here is a sample data set."}, {"start_seconds": 27.68, "end_seconds": 33.52, "text": "Sales of three stores across 3 months."}, {"start_seconds": 31.44, "end_seconds": 35.96, "text": "Notice that each month is a separate"}, {"start_seconds": 33.52, "end_seconds": 38.4, "text": "column, and that's a wide format. But,"}, {"start_seconds": 35.96, "end_seconds": 40.76, "text": "for analysis or visualization, we often"}, {"start_seconds": 38.4, "end_seconds": 43.0, "text": "need a long format. One column for"}, {"start_seconds": 40.76, "end_seconds": 45.48, "text": "months and one for values. And that's"}, {"start_seconds": 43.0, "end_seconds": 47.56, "text": "where melt helps."}, {"start_seconds": 45.48, "end_seconds": 49.88, "text": "Let's do an example and transform this"}, {"start_seconds": 47.56, "end_seconds": 51.64, "text": "data from wide to long format using"}, {"start_seconds": 49.88, "end_seconds": 54.72, "text": "Pandas melt method."}, {"start_seconds": 51.64, "end_seconds": 57.72, "text": "Let me create a data frame called melt."}, {"start_seconds": 54.72, "end_seconds": 57.72, "text": "pd.melt"}, {"start_seconds": 58.32, "end_seconds": 63.4, "text": "We will pass the data frame DF."}, {"start_seconds": 61.92, "end_seconds": 66.84, "text": "And then,"}, {"start_seconds": 63.4, "end_seconds": 69.6, "text": "we will use id_vars"}, {"start_seconds": 66.84, "end_seconds": 69.6, "text": "parameter."}, {"start_seconds": 70.08, "end_seconds": 75.48, "text": "And we will"}, {"start_seconds": 72.28, "end_seconds": 77.0, "text": "pass the variable store."}, {"start_seconds": 75.48, "end_seconds": 79.44, "text": "Now,"}, {"start_seconds": 77.0, "end_seconds": 81.28, "text": "what it is going to do is"}, {"start_seconds": 79.44, "end_seconds": 84.76, "text": "that we are telling Pandas to keep the"}, {"start_seconds": 81.28, "end_seconds": 87.2, "text": "store column as is, and and melt all"}, {"start_seconds": 84.76, "end_seconds": 89.48, "text": "other columns into two columns, variable"}, {"start_seconds": 87.2, "end_seconds": 91.84, "text": "and value. Let's run the code and see"}, {"start_seconds": 89.48, "end_seconds": 91.84, "text": "that."}, {"start_seconds": 92.24, "end_seconds": 94.88, "text": "melt"}, {"start_seconds": 95.28, "end_seconds": 99.56, "text": "So, you can see here, the store column"}, {"start_seconds": 97.64, "end_seconds": 102.64, "text": "is as is,"}, {"start_seconds": 99.56, "end_seconds": 106.04, "text": "whereas the columns Jan_Sales,"}, {"start_seconds": 102.64, "end_seconds": 108.88, "text": "Feb_Sales, and Mar_Sales"}, {"start_seconds": 106.04, "end_seconds": 111.12, "text": "have been converted into a long format"}, {"start_seconds": 108.88, "end_seconds": 113.0, "text": "with a column name variable,"}, {"start_seconds": 111.12, "end_seconds": 116.2, "text": "whereas"}, {"start_seconds": 113.0, "end_seconds": 118.96, "text": "it also created a new column value for"}, {"start_seconds": 116.2, "end_seconds": 121.04, "text": "the numerical value parts. And this is"}, {"start_seconds": 118.96, "end_seconds": 123.84, "text": "how one can convert the data from to"}, {"start_seconds": 121.04, "end_seconds": 126.0, "text": "long format using melt method."}, {"start_seconds": 123.84, "end_seconds": 128.8, "text": "Let's do another example where we are"}, {"start_seconds": 126.0, "end_seconds": 131.48, "text": "going to rename those variables"}, {"start_seconds": 128.8, "end_seconds": 135.0, "text": "variable and value as per our choice."}, {"start_seconds": 131.48, "end_seconds": 135.0, "text": "DF underscore melt"}, {"start_seconds": 135.52, "end_seconds": 138.52, "text": "pd.melt"}, {"start_seconds": 138.64, "end_seconds": 142.32, "text": "Let's pass the data frame DF."}, {"start_seconds": 143.68, "end_seconds": 150.64, "text": "id underscore bars"}, {"start_seconds": 147.44, "end_seconds": 150.64, "text": "equal to store"}, {"start_seconds": 152.64, "end_seconds": 158.12, "text": "then"}, {"start_seconds": 154.32, "end_seconds": 159.6, "text": "var underscore name This is for renaming"}, {"start_seconds": 158.12, "end_seconds": 162.8, "text": "the variable"}, {"start_seconds": 159.6, "end_seconds": 165.8, "text": "from variable to our uh"}, {"start_seconds": 162.8, "end_seconds": 168.52, "text": "column name of our choice."}, {"start_seconds": 165.8, "end_seconds": 168.52, "text": "month"}, {"start_seconds": 171.44, "end_seconds": 177.12, "text": "then value"}, {"start_seconds": 174.4, "end_seconds": 180.08, "text": "equal to sales"}, {"start_seconds": 177.12, "end_seconds": 180.08, "text": "and let's run the code."}, {"start_seconds": 181.2, "end_seconds": 186.76, "text": "Oh, sorry."}, {"start_seconds": 182.8, "end_seconds": 186.76, "text": "value underscore name"}, {"start_seconds": 188.48, "end_seconds": 191.4, "text": "Let's see the output."}, {"start_seconds": 192.64, "end_seconds": 197.24, "text": "So, you can see here we can rename these"}, {"start_seconds": 195.16, "end_s